            </exercise>
           
      </section>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
        <para id="para-00044"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_8_10_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Working with Expressions of the Form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></title>
        <para id="para-00045">You have factored and solved many different types of <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00006">quadratic equations</term>, but the leading <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00007">coefficient</term> of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> term was often 1.</para>
        <para id="para-00046">Let’s look at the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00008">factored form</term> of a more complex expression to better understand the process.</para>
        <para id="para-00047"><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00048">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00009">standard form</term>.</para>
        <para id="para-00049">To find the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00010">quadratic expression</term> in standard form, use the distributive property of multiplication over addition, or FOIL.</para>
        <para id="para-00050"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00051">Now, let’s try to go the other direction from standard form to factored form.</para>
        <para id="para-00052"><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00053">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in factored form.</para>
        <para id="para-00054">Since the leading coefficient is 2, we know the factored form must have the structure:</para>
        <para id="para-00055"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00056">Since the constant term is +15, the two missing numbers in the factored form must have a product of 15.</para>
        <para id="para-00057">The possibilities include:</para>
        <para id="para-00058">+1 and +15 +3 and +5 -1 and -15 -3 and -5</para>
        <para id="para-00059">Since the middle term, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, is positive, we know that only the positive factors need to be considered.</para>
        <para id="para-00060">Since the two factors are already different inside the parentheses, the order in which we place the numbers is important. We will try both, if necessary.</para>
        <para id="para-00061">Let’s try <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00062"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>17</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> not equivalent to the original expression</para>
        <para id="para-00063">Try reordering the same numbers.</para>
        <para id="para-00064"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:red">5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>31</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> not equivalent to the original expression</para>
        <para id="para-00065">Let’s try <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00066"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> not equivalent to the original expression</para>
        <para id="para-00067">Try reordering the same numbers.</para>
        <para id="para-00068"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn style="color:blue">5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi style="color:red">✓</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to the original expression</para>
        <para id="para-00069">So, the factored form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Working with Expressions of the Form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></title>
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
            <problem id="prob-00010">
              <para id="para-00070">Find the factored form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
              <para id="para-00071">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00010">
              <para id="para-00072">Here is how to find the factored form:</para>
              <para id="para-00073">The factored form will have the structure: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
              <para id="para-00074">The factors of -4 are:</para>
              <para id="para-00075">-4 and 1 4 and -1 -2 and 2</para>
              <para id="para-00076">Try -4 and 1.</para>
              <para id="para-00077"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> not equivalent to the original expression</para>
              <para id="para-00078">Try reordering.</para>
              <para id="para-00079"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mi style="color:red">✓</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math>equivalent to the original expression</para>
              <para id="para-00080">The factored form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>